{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DarknessTimeAndDeath","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/daemon(_:autostart:perform:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopFuse(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuseRemaining(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startDaemon(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopDaemon(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/isDaemonActive(_:)"],"anchor":"Time-Light-and-Death","generated":true,"title":"Time, Light, and Death"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/timedevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimedEvent","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DarknessTimeAndDeath","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timer names are bare strings wherever they are unambiguous. Two owners"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the game and a bundle, or two bundles) may both declare one name: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bootstrap moves each bundle-owned declaration into its namespace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Clock.roam\""},{"type":"text","text":") while the game’s own stays bare, and a body running for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its owner resolves the bare literal it declared against that owner first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and friends). A host game addresses a bundle’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collided timer by the qualified name."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timers tick once per typed command, at the very end of the turn (after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the world’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":"\/each-turn rules): fuses first, then daemons, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"group in name order. They tick on refused turns (world time passes) but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not on parse errors, meta commands, or once the game has ended. A timer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"started earlier in the turn ticks at the end of that same turn — so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fuse(after: 1)"},{"type":"text","text":" started by a rule fires as that very turn ends. A timer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"started or restarted "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"while the tick runs"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — by a fuse or daemon body, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by anything a body calls — is a turn behind that: the tick skips it, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first ticks at the end of the next turn, wherever its name sorts."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimedEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"title":"TimedEvent","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:6Gnusto10TimedEventV"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A named timed event, declared in a game or bundle "},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block: a fuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(fires once, N turns after it is started) or a daemon (runs at the end of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every turn while active). The body is registered at bootstrap and never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serialized; only the schedule — name → turns remaining, or the active"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flag — lives in "},{"code":"WorldState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it saves and restores like any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state and a restore re-binds it to the declared body by name."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Plugins":{"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/plugins","title":"Plugins","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Package a reusable game system as an importable unit of verbs and rules."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TimedEvent":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/timedevent","title":"TimedEvent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A named timed event, declared in a game or bundle "},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block: a fuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(fires once, N turns after it is started) or a daemon (runs at the end of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every turn while active). The body is registered at bootstrap and never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serialized; only the schedule — name → turns remaining, or the active"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flag — lives in "},{"code":"WorldState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it saves and restores like any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state and a restore re-binds it to the declared body by name."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent"},"doc://Gnusto/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/stopDaemon(_:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stopDaemon"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/stopdaemon(_:)","kind":"symbol","title":"stopDaemon(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stops the named daemon. A no-op if it isn’t running."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopDaemon(_:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/isDaemonActive(_:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isDaemonActive"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/isdaemonactive(_:)","title":"isDaemonActive(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the named daemon is currently active.